        {
          "sid": "clothing-t1-s01",
          "c": "我想買件新衫。",
          "j": "ngo5 soeng2 maai5 gin6 san1 saam1.",
          "e": "I want to buy a new top.",
          "note": "A short adjective attaches straight to the noun, no 嘅 (ge3) needed — 新衫 (san1 saam1) \"new top\", 舊鞋 (gau6 haai4) \"old shoes\". (Longer or coloured descriptions take 嘅 (ge3): 綠色嘅褲 (luk6 sik1 ge3 fu3).) 件 (gin6) is the top's classifier.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我想",
              "j": "ngo5 soeng2",
              "e": "I want to"
            },
            {
              "c": "買",
              "j": "maai5",
              "e": "buy"
            },
            {
              "c": "件",
              "j": "gin6",
              "e": "(classifier)"
            },
            {
              "c": "新衫",
              "j": "san1 saam1",
              "e": "new top"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "clothing-t1-s02",
          "c": "呢對鞋幾錢呀？",
          "j": "ni1 deoi3 haai4 gei2 cin2 aa3?",
          "e": "How much are these shoes?",
          "note": "對 (deoi3) is the classifier for things that come in pairs — 一對鞋 (jat1 deoi3 haai4) \"a pair of shoes\", 一對襪 (jat1 deoi3 mat6) \"a pair of socks\", 一對筷子 (jat1 deoi3 faai3 zi2) \"chopsticks\".",
