              "c": "外套",
              "j": "ngoi6 tou3",
              "e": "coat"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "clothing-t1-s04",
          "c": "你條裙好靚！",
          "j": "nei5 tiu4 kwan4 hou2 leng3!",
          "e": "Your dress is so pretty!",
          "note": "靚 (leng3) is the Cantonese for \"pretty / good-looking / nice\" — 好靚 (hou2 leng3) \"really pretty\", for people, clothes, food, or views. A word you'll use constantly. 條 (tiu4) is the classifier for the skirt.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "你",
              "j": "nei5",
              "e": "your"
            },
            {
              "c": "條",
              "j": "tiu4",
              "e": "(classifier)"
            },
            {
              "c": "裙",
              "j": "kwan4",
              "e": "dress"
            },
            {
              "c": "好靚",
              "j": "hou2 leng3",
              "e": "very pretty"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "clothing-t1-s05",
          "c": "我搵唔到對襪。",
          "j": "ngo5 wan2 m4 dou2 deoi3 mat6.",
          "e": "I can't find my socks.",
          "note": "搵 (wan2) is Cantonese for \"look for / find\" — Mandarin uses 找 (zaau2). Add 唔到 (m4 dou2) \"can't manage to\" after a verb for failure — 搵唔到 (wan2 m4 dou2) \"can't find\", 買唔到 (maai5 m4 dou2) \"can't get\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "I"
            },
            {
              "c": "搵唔到",
